  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1236 PM Friday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonal temperatures and pleasant conditions will \ngradually trend above normal towards the middle to latter part of \nnext week.\n\nAn early season Nor'easter presently over the western Atlantic will \ntrack towards New England this weekend and linger over that region \ninto early next week. In time, the system will eventually get kicked \neastward as ridging develops over the central and southern US and \ntracks eastward into the Carolinas during the middle to latter part \nof next week.\n\nGorgeous weather is expected the rest of today through early next \nweek. Daytime highs are favored in the upper 70s to some low 80s \nduring this stretch. These temperatures are right about average. \nCorrespondingly, dry air with dewpoints in the 40s will make for \nthat comfortable fall feel. Low temperatures tonight and Saturday \nnight are favored to be in the mid 40s to low 50s, about 5-10 \ndegrees below normal. Even a few low 40s cannot be ruled out in \noutlying areas of the Piedmont tonight.\n\nWe can expect a gradual warming trend toward the middle to latter \npart of next week as ridging builds in from the west. Rising \nthicknesses and heights will favor a trend to above normal highs in \nthe mid to upper 80s Wednesday through Friday.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Dry weather overall, with a slight signal for \nincreased rain chances late next week or weekend.\n\nOverall dry conditions are expected through the middle of next week. \nA dry northwest flow will exist at mid-levels through early next \nweek, effectively shutting off our moisture source for rain. We \ncould see some increased clouds Sunday and Monday as the Nor'easter \ntracks into New England and portions of the Mid-Atlantic states, but \nany rain stays off to our north and east.\n\nOur best chance of a return to unsettled weather may not come until \nlate next week Friday or the following weekend. Ensemble guidance is \nmixed on the overall pattern tied to an approaching system. Overall \nconfidence is thus low, dependent upon the degree of ridging \nexpected late next week. For now, our forecast calls for low-end \nrain chances by Friday.",
